WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.370
I'm just here with my good friend Elmo.

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.203
Yeah.

3
00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.250
I know-
Just hanging out.

4
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.460
Yes, because we both have talk shows.

5
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.480
That's true!

6
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.111
Which is so wonderful.

7
00:00:09.111 --> 00:00:11.520
Elmo's learning a lot, this is a much bigger talk show,

8
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.590
this is a swanky place.
(audience laughs)

9
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.050
We just do Elmo's talk show in his apartment.

10
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.480
I gotta tell you, I know your set,

11
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.350
'cause I've been there firsthand and it's magnificent.

12
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.124
You have a big slide.

13
00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.594
Yeah, but Elmo's not sure how we got it into the apartment

14
00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.530
and Elmo's not really sure how we're gonna get it out.

15
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.630
But we do what we can with what we have.

16
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.330
I think your show is gonna be on for so long,

17
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.960
you're never gonna have to worry about it.

18
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.197
Really?
(audience cheers and applauds)

19
00:00:42.197 --> 00:00:45.610
Well, Elmo, someone who's coming on

20
00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.470
is someone that I really look to

21
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.950
as a really wonderful interviewer.

22
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.950
Oh, cool!

23
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.870
Yeah, she's a young journalist

24
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.940
and someone I hold very dear to my heart

25
00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.890
and she gave us so many amazing moments last season.

26
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.920
And here's our little love letter

27
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.993
to our member of The Drew Crew.

28
00:01:04.835 --> 00:01:05.780
(upbeat music)

29
00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.532
She is a budding young journalist.

30
00:01:07.532 --> 00:01:09.250
I love asking questions.

31
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.882
And an internet sensation.

32
00:01:10.882 --> 00:01:15.510
I'm tell you guys a joke, bit's kind of inappropriate.

33
00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.940
She's the eight year old girl

34
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.530
behind 7 Questions with Emmy.

35
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.040
The best journalist in the business.

36
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.470
And a very special member of Drew's Crew,

37
00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.460
it's Emmy Eaton.

38
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.382
Are you ready to get into some stories?

39
00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:28.130
Yes, yes, yes, I'm so excited.

40
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.200
She's already interviewed Keith Morrison,

41
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.540
Lester Holt, Dr. Oz, and on our show last season,

42
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.980
she grilled Seth Meyers and Willie Geist.

43
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.520
Seth, is it really hard to make people laugh every day?

44
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.390
Only my wife.
(Drew laughs)

45
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.370
Armed with her quick wit and curiosity,

46
00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.846
Emmy is here to deliver all the good news.

47
00:01:46.846 --> 00:01:51.846
We need more Emmy. The world needs more Emmy.

48
00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:54.362
(audience applauding)

49
00:01:54.362 --> 00:01:56.080
And the dream comes true!

50
00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.330
Please welcome, for the first time ever,

51
00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.459
in the actual studio, live and in person, it's Emmy Eaton.

52
00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:06.858
(audience cheering and applauding)

53
00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:09.390
Ah, Emmy, I'm so glad that you're finally here

54
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.330
in New York City!

55
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.430
I'm so glad I finally got to see you in person Drew.

56
00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.340
Oh my gosh, I've been waiting for this moment

57
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.970
and I can't think of a more special occasion,

58
00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.940
than to have our first time in person

59
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.694
get to be then with none other than Elmo.

60
00:02:23.694 --> 00:02:25.944
Hi Elmo!
Hi, hi, hi!

61
00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:27.047
Nice to meet you.

62
00:02:27.047 --> 00:02:31.580
You too. My little brother Elliot loves you-

63
00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.107
Really?
So much, yes.

64
00:02:33.107 --> 00:02:35.774
Hi Elliot, Elmo loves you too.

65
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.260
Okay. I mean, I heard that you had some questions for Elmo

66
00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.280
and I'd like you to take over this interview.

67
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.990
Okay.
Okay.

68
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.030
Question number one, how old are you?

69
00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.479
Forty four.
(Drew and Emmy giggling)

70
00:02:48.479 --> 00:02:50.047
No, Elmo's just kidding! No, Elmo's three and a half.

71
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.640
Question number two.
Okay.

72
00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.390
What's your favorite food?

73
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.645
Hmm.

74
00:02:57.645 --> 00:03:01.523
Well, if Elmo's being a good monster, Elmo says apples.

75
00:03:03.346 --> 00:03:07.465
But don't tell anybody, pizza.

76
00:03:07.465 --> 00:03:09.625
(Elmo and Emmy laugh)

77
00:03:09.625 --> 00:03:11.160
You and Ross Matthews, Elmo.

78
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.105
Really?
Mm-hmm.

79
00:03:12.105 --> 00:03:12.938
(Elmo laughs)

80
00:03:12.938 --> 00:03:15.740
You're gonna have to come and try New York pizza,

81
00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.870
it's really good.

82
00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.170
Oh, okay, maybe we can go for some pizza.

83
00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.560
Yeah!
Okay, cool.

84
00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.120
Who is your best friend on Sesame Street?

85
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.800
See Emmy, this is a very difficult question.

86
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.780
Because if Elmo says Cookie Monster,

87
00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.600
Grover says, "Hey, wait a minute,

88
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.450
you said Cookie Monster was your favorite?"

89
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.963
So Elmo loves everybody equally.

90
00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.690
I think that's a great answer, actually. I really do.

91
00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.223
Because I think you don't wanna hurt anybody's feelings.

92
00:03:42.223 --> 00:03:44.094
And how can you decide?

93
00:03:44.094 --> 00:03:45.280
Yeah.
I know.

94
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.790
Big Bird, Bert and Ernie, Rosita, Abby, there's so many.

95
00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.180
I agree.
Yeah.

96
00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.220 line:15%
I have a bunch of best friends too,

97
00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.330 line:15%
and they always asked me if they're my favorite,

98
00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.610 line:15%
and I say all of them.

99
00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.015 line:15%
Yeah, that's right, you can't say, right?

100
00:03:59.015 --> 00:03:59.848
Yeah.

101
00:03:59.848 --> 00:04:02.410
And you love everybody for different reasons.

102
00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.528
Yeah. What makes you laugh?

103
00:04:05.528 --> 00:04:08.230
Well, Elmo's friends make Elmo laugh.

104
00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.130
Yeah.

105
00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:12.040
Yeah, Cookie Monster makes Elmo laugh, Big Bird.

106
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.107
And you know, Elmo's ticklish, that's kind of Elmo's thing,

107
00:04:15.107 --> 00:04:17.850
so that makes Elmo laugh too.

108
00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.760
My little brother makes me laugh,

109
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.330
because he always, when your show comes on,

110
00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.507
he always goes, "Elmo, Elmo!"

111
00:04:23.507 --> 00:04:26.840
And then he thinks you're there in real life,

112
00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.060
so then he is like, "Come give me a hug!"

113
00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.941
And then he gets so sad that you're not there.

114
00:04:32.941 --> 00:04:36.233
(Elmo cries)
That makes Elmo sad too.

115
00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:37.936
Elliot, Elmo wants you to know

116
00:04:37.936 --> 00:04:40.170
that you can come to Sesame Street anytime

117
00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.410
and Elmo with give you a hug.

118
00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.732
What advice do you have for me?

119
00:04:44.732 --> 00:04:46.153
Advice?

120
00:04:46.153 --> 00:04:49.323
Boy, well Elmo thinks you're doing really well already.

121
00:04:49.323 --> 00:04:51.270
Elmo thinks you have great questions,

122
00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.610
you have really good listening and Elmo just thinks

123
00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.960
you should keep doing what you're doing,

124
00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.640
'cause you're gonna go really far.

125
00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.860
Thank you Elmo.
You're welcome!

126
00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.130
I have to agree.

127
00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.150
And I think it's a miracle that all three of us

128
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.970
are together, because we're all curious.

129
00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.530
Yeah.
That's true.

130
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.170
And if we can bring that to our shows,

131
00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.330
then we can be very good at our jobs

132
00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.650
and ask people questions.

133
00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.870
And maybe when those people give answers,

134
00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.930
we can all have really good takeaways from them.

135
00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.629 line:15%
Yeah.
Very true.

136
00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:22.462 line:15%
Yeah.

137
00:05:22.462 --> 00:05:24.040 line:15%
Elmo can't say it better than that, that was perfect.

138
00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.013 line:15%
Oh my goodness. Well, thank you!

139
00:05:25.013 --> 00:05:26.386 line:15%
That was perfect!
(audience applauding)

140
00:05:26.386 --> 00:05:30.802
Thank you Elmo and thank you Emmy, my love!

141
00:05:30.802 --> 00:05:32.390
Emmy, yay!
(audience applauding)

142
00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:36.180
The Not So Late Show With Elmo returns on September 30th

143
00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.468 line:15%
and is available to stream on HBO Max.

144
00:05:39.468 --> 00:05:42.551 line:15%
(upbeat theme music)

